  "witness": "reference band uses its bound participant rectangle with the same header/padding rule",
  "derivation": "Region (Process_1, reference-band) -> Band_1 (0,250000,600000,90000); tokens hw 20000, p 5000, g 10000, mh 60000; contentLeft 25000. Both references anchor on Task_1 (centre x 200000): Ref_1 left 175000, Ref_2 collides with 225000+10000 -> 235000. RH = max(60000, 50000+10000) = 60000 <= 90000; row [250000, 310000], cy = 250000 + max(25000, 30000) = 280000: objects at y 255000. The collaboration plane gives semanticRootId Collab_1. Row rule (spec \u00a74.3): items in \u00a77.2 placement order; footprint max(object, label) width; left = anchor centre - footprint/2 when the anchor is shown, else contentLeft or previous right + gap; clamp to contentLeft; collision shifts right; one row at the top of the support body [Ly, Ly+RH], RH = max(minHeight, max(object+label) + 2 padding) (harmonization K2); every object centre lies on one line cy = Ly + max(A, (RH + A - B)/2), A = max h/2, B = max(h/2 + label height), so the union of the stacks is centred in the row (DESIGN \u00a79.4 'align centers on one IO row'); exact rationals, one roundEven per output coordinate. The profile is re-pinned to the lot-4 extension packages neutral-render-descriptors/1 and neutral-render-base/1 (tests/profile_render/expected/artifacts/), which admit every native type of the tree.",
